  "sesan": "Sesan",
  "forKhmerFarmers": "Technology for Khmer farmers",
  "aboutQuestion": "Why does an agricultural country still need to import agricultural products?",
  "aboutQuestionAnswer": "This simple question inspired us to create Sesan.",
  "aboutLandTitle": "Farmland — a valuable national asset",
  "aboutLandContent": "Cambodia is an agricultural country with fertile soil, sufficient water and year-round sunshine.\n\nYet we still import lemongrass, garlic, fertilizer and farming supplies. Foreign companies operate large farms on Cambodian land while profits flow abroad.\n\nMeanwhile, many children of farming families leave home to work on other people's land. This is a challenge we can change together.",
  "aboutFarmersTitle": "Farmers — the people who sustain life",
  "aboutFarmersContent": "Every meal we eat comes from the hard work of farmers. Rice, vegetables, fish and meat are produced by people who work through heat and rain to feed us all.\n\nYet many food producers live with financial hardship and debt while intermediaries often earn more.\n\nThis imbalance in the supply chain is something we must work together to change.",
  "aboutWorkValueTitle": "The value of farmers' work",
  "aboutWorkValueContent": "The work of farmers is invaluable because farmers feed society. No amount of money can sustain life without food.\n\nSesan was created with an understanding of every step from farm to table, serving as a direct bridge between producers and consumers.",
  "aboutMissionTitle": "Sesan — our mission",
  "aboutMissionContent": "Sesan was not created only for profit. Our mission is to:\n\n✦ Help farmers sell directly without unfair intermediary margins\n\n✦ Give buyers fresh, safe farm products at fair prices\n\n✦ Keep more income in the hands of Cambodian farmers and strengthen families and communities\n\n✦ Elevate Cambodian agriculture as a source of national pride.",
  "aboutThanksTitle": "Thank you",
  "aboutThanksContent": "We thank every farmer who rises early and works in the fields to provide food for people across the country.\n\nFarmers are the quiet heroes who support our national economy. Sesan will continue standing with them to protect their interests and the value of their work.",
  "aboutSlogan": "Cambodian soil, Cambodian hands, Cambodian products, on Cambodian tables\n\nSesan — agricultural technology for the future of Khmer farmers",
